	In a recent game, I had a pet dwarf, acquired via scroll of taming.
It turned out he was wielding a cursed pickaxe, and I was interested in
getting it away from him.  But how?  A whip won't work on a cursed
weapon.  I guess I could have polymorphed into a nymph and stolen it
away, but that's a little harder to arrange.  Is there any way to
uncurse a pet's weapon?

	This game was a fun one - at one point I had two large dogs, a dwarf
king, and three elves following me around!  For some reason scrolls of
taming were as common as dirt this game.  I eventually lost one elf and
one dog, but a large dog, dwarf king, and two elf kings is still a
pretty good band.  I like intelligent, item-using pets, and elf kings
top out at level 13, with over 100HP, and mine had AC around -4.  I was
a little shocked at what quick work my pets made of the Minetown priest,
not to mention the shopkeepers - sorry, Izchak, I tried, I really did.
But when one of your pets is a dwarf with a cursed pickaxe you can't
take away, it's kind of hard to keep them out of anyplace!

	As for the YASD: the only problem with so many pets is that they eat
everything.  No problem - I'd just pray for my dinner, and grab the rare
corpse where I could get to it before they did.  And then I ate a dwarf
corpse...forgetting that I was one.  "You cannibal!  You will regret
this!"  And regret it I did.  Food was in very short supply, and with
Quetzalcoatl angry at me, praying was out.  I resorted to attacking
peaceful gnomes in the hopes of eating their corpses, which probably
didn't help matters.  I ate my tripe, I ate my lizard corpse, I even ate
my wolfbane.  I got lucky once when a rothe fell in a pit and died, so
my pets wouldn't go after it, but it was only postponing the inevitable.
But I do see that I left bones, so some lucky Hearse user is going to
have fun with this one.

